From 51185c460a4be78e713f4ed3db54987319b1834f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 07:30:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] perf(net): a stealth page's subresources use the shared cache
 and request sharing

The stealth client fetched every script, stylesheet, image and font
afresh: no reuse of a response the server marked cacheable, and no
sharing of identical requests in flight, both of which the plain client
does. A stealth page (the mode the host runs) re-downloaded its shared
scripts on every navigation and sent one request per copy of a resource
its frames and documents asked for at once. Its subresource GETs now go
through the same loader; nine requests for one cacheable script make one
transaction, and observers still see nine.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
